  "description": "Overview: Calling all tech enthusiasts and finance aficionados! The Finance and Economics Society of NSUT is excited to bring you Fintechstico , the flagship FinTech Hackathon of Consilium’26 . We invite aspiring innovators to come together and participate in a competition focused on solving real-world challenges faced by people in their everyday lives. Get ready for 2 days of intense ideation, prototyping, and pitching as you turn your ideas into impactful solutions and put your skills to the test. Guidelines: The hackathon will be conducted offline , and all shortlisted teams are required to be physically present at NSUT Main Campus, Dwarka during the event. Participants must upload their CV, past work, GitHub profile, portfolio, or any other relevant work that they believe strengthens their application and improves their chances of being shortlisted for the preliminary round. Note: Every team member must upload their individual CV/Portfolio/GitHub or relevant past work to be eligible for consideration in the Preliminary Round. Rules: The event is open to students from all colleges. Cross-college teams are permitted. Each team can have a maximum of four members. Individual participation is not permitted; teams must have at least two members. A participant cannot be a member of more than one team. Dummy or false registrations are strictly prohibited. FES reserves the right to take decisions regarding the conduct and management of the event, and all participating teams must abide by such decisions. FES reserves the right to modify, amend, or update the terms and conditions of the competition whenever required. By participating in the competition, all participants will be considered to have accepted and agreed to abide by these rules and any additional requirements communicated through the competition material. Any violation of the rules may result in immediate disqualification.",
