ents from all colleges.</li>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\">Cross-college teams are permitted.</li>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\">Each team can have a maximum of four members.</li>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\">Individual participation is not permitted; teams must have at least two members.</li>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\">A participant cannot be a member of more than one team.</li>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\">Dummy or false registrations are strictly prohibited.</li>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\">FES reserves the right to take decisions regarding the conduct and management of the event, and all participating teams must abide by such decisions.</li>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\">FES reserves the right to modify, amend, or update the terms and conditions of the competition whenever required. By participating in the competition, all participants will be considered to have accepted and agreed to abide by these rules and any additional requirements communicated through the competition material.</li>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\">Any violation of the rules may result in immediate disqualification.</li>\n</ul>",
